{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested on member/presence draft 2 at exact a52734e36350b7432c967481ea830cdcb07019da, tree b8159795fb8112c378f11c517007fccd1e6c7044. Primary 31e9bff2 read FIRST IN FULL, all 378 lines. Complete design review; the remaining findings are together below.\n\nF3 (P2), primary 199–202 and 219–223: state the readable native source for the recorded arrival/leave entry number. “N is the item's revision entry” does not identify a field or bounded read that supplies that entry. Native Item has an opening position/id and an item revision, not the entry position of its latest change (contract/read.ts:41–58). The actual fold raises an existing item's revision by one per changing entry (derive/fold.ts:164–165), independently of that entry's sequence. For example, an item opened at entry 8/revision 1 and next moved by arrive at entry 108 has revision 2: neither opening entry 8 nor revision 2 identifies the report at 108. The same issue applies to “left ... at entry N.” Require the second G3 presence item/projection to retain and expose the actual arrival/leave fact or entry position, with its scope binding, and use that for both expressions and the late-opening witness. Alternatively display the room/state with entry provenance unavailable, or explicitly label an item revision as a revision. This asks for a source contract for B3, not a schema implementation in this documentation head.\n\nF4 (P2), primary 141–150: distinguish an unavailable optional removal-provenance read from a complete last-100 read with no match. The new budget and “removal entry not in the last 100 entries” sentence address an older removal only when that bounded read successfully completes. They do not specify the expression when history access is refused, the read fails or cannot complete within its existing bounds. Such an answer cannot establish that the removal is outside the window. Add a separate sentence such as “removal entry unavailable” for those outcomes, retain known identity and removed state, and reserve the no-match sentence for a complete captured window with no matching removal. Include that failure branch beside the already specified 5,000-entry-old example; do not add an unbounded lookup.\n\nConclusion 1 — fidelity: draft 2 substantially addresses the earlier findings. F1's occupancy error is removed: recorded presence waits for the application's persistent Site item in the second G3 head; the last-100 projection is explicitly recent activity with unknown coverage, not occupancy. Full room-subject mapping, one room per member/site and arrive A → arrive B → leave A semantics are stated, including a permitted named wrong-room refusal. Recorded expressions carry no status, note, freshness or lease, and B3 waits for the second head. F2's “removed since entry N” label is replaced by “removed” from item state, with optional bounded record-screen provenance. The two findings above complete the remaining provenance contracts.\n\nConclusion 2 — correctness and witnesses: the three independent layers and their unavailable expressions, controller attribution, bounded resolution table/overflow, typed party/signer inputs, kit-only membership controls and package member-open-only API remain sound directions. Source checks confirm native item revision versus entry sequence, remove-member's state-only effect, the journal window grammar, and the inherited live declaration. Enter without a status is permitted by that declaration; Enter/Renew/Leave still require actual ownership/session/generation/expected judgments. Renewal is correctly deferred to B4 and view_read supplies none. The surface boundary remains a tested API authority boundary, explicitly not hostile-code isolation. Design traces checked include the late arrival outside the window, move then old-room leave, unavailable room binding, old removal, failed provenance, and a later item change whose revision differs from its entry. These are source/design checks, not executed runtime or UI acceptance.\n\nConclusion 3 — validation cost and limits: documentation-only head. Compared every Git mode/blob leaf with its declared authored Main 4d8c878c4c40f6d4399f2bcf5567125bb3ba1bc8/tree e568c5d498e974bacd49e135e452e8b5a24edbee: exactly this note changes; 2239 leaves are unchanged and the candidate has 2240 leaves. Only this note differs from reviewed draft 1 e00abdb7. The older authored base is explicit, so later Main runtime differences are not new changes in this note. Whitespace passes; exact-path artifact query is exhausted with one fresh candidate artifact and assigned implementation binding is prepared. No source/tests changed, so docs/testing.md's documentation-only exception applies: no gate or whole suite was rerun. Scratch /private/tmp/checker-member-presence-draft2-1_ybee53 contains exact note.md and validation.json (note SHA256 65e016428e886f6da2fbf20ae3a55392f73081070d79a20e6878913d9909f405).\n\nNo further findings in this complete pass. D1 mockups, B1/B2 implementation, B3 persistent source and its actual native/browser witnesses, B4 live executor/renewal, publication and deployment remain separate work. No runtime, hosting, physical device or hostile-code isolation outcome is claimed.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:31e9bff2ac9c9702c9b6682bff8806d091ed135d","binding":"assigned","head":"a52734e36350b7432c967481ea830cdcb07019da","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:92821e805836240d39a626d78dfb514d54999b54\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:45d75285ba181142cec9f66a640987a0b44093bc\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:16b45b2c5b32b45773211a71e4f5adb3e27f862b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}